## Lost Limb Riders — Document Lifecycle Procedure

**Document ID:** ADM-PROC-001
**Document Title:** Document Lifecycle Procedure
**Department:** Administration
**Document Type:** PROC
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** August 12, 2026
**Review Date:** August 2027
**Document Owner:** Director of Administration
**Approving Authority:** Executive Director
**Supersedes:** None
**Related Documents:** GOV-POL-001 (Document Control); ADM-PROC-002 (Change Control); FIN-CTRL-001 (Approval Matrix); MASTER-INDEX.md §11–12
**Related Forms:** None
**Record Classification:** Administrative
**Retention Requirement:** Permanent (while in force)

---

## 1. Purpose

To create, approve, publish, maintain, and retire controlled documents consistently.

## 2. Lifecycle Stages

### Stage 1 — Identify Need
A policy, procedure, checklist, form, or register is needed when a workflow exists without documentation or a control gap is found. Any authorized person may propose a new document.

### Stage 2 — Draft
- Use the standard header block (GOV-POL-001 §4).
- Assign the next Document ID in the department’s series (check the document register / index first to avoid duplicates).
- Link the document to its governing policy, procedure, checklist, form, and register.
- Use the organization’s style (existing handbooks style guide).

### Stage 3 — Review
- Route to the department head and affected functions for comment.
- Compliance-sensitive documents are reviewed against the source authorities (CMP-REF-001).

### Stage 4 — Approve
- Approval authority per FIN-CTRL-001 and GOV-POL-001 §7. Policies need Board approval; procedures/forms need the responsible department head or Executive Director.

### Stage 5 — Publish
- Place the document in its department folder in the transactional layer.
- Update the department index and the forms index (13-FORMS-AND-TEMPLATES) if a form.
- Update the MASTER-INDEX document set table.

### Stage 6 — Use
- Operators use the current version only. Superseded versions are not used for operations.

### Stage 7 — Review
- The owner reviews on or before the Review Date, confirms accuracy, and renews or initiates a change.

### Stage 8 — Retire
- Retire per ADM-PROC-002. Mark the document Superseded, retain it (do not delete), update all references, and record the change.

## 3. Version Rules

- Substantive change → new minor or major version.
- New version sets `Supersedes` to the prior Document ID.
- The prior document is marked superseded with the replacement ID.

## 4. Common Mistakes to Avoid

- Reusing a Document ID
- Creating a form with no procedure
- Editing a published document without versioning
- Committing completed confidential forms to the repository

---

**End of Procedure.**
